+    never scheduled at all, finished by an earlier run, or archived since. Every bundle name
+    under ``results/`` or ``results/completed/`` is read once, where :func:`member_path`
+    finds it: the active bundle, else the archived one (#171). A group is each connected
+    set of the relation. A brief that cannot be read (unreadable, not UTF-8) declares
+    nothing here: a bundle of the run fails on its own reads elsewhere, and one outside it
